An HTML attribute is written once, whatever its case

```
{type=text}
a. alpha
.
<ol type="a">
  <li>alpha</li>
</ol>
```

```
{start=9}
3. x
.
<ol start="3">
  <li>x</li>
</ol>
```

```
![a](/u.png){alt=z}
.
<img src="/u.png" alt="a">
```

```
[a](/u "T"){TITLE=t}
.
<p><a href="/u" title="T">a</a></p>
```

```
{start=9}
1. x
.
<ol start="9">
  <li>x</li>
</ol>
```

```
{K=1 k=2}
para
.
<p K="2">para</p>
```

```
{CLASS=z}
::: |
verse
:::
.
<div CLASS="z line-block">
  <p>verse</p>
</div>
```

```
[x]{.a CLASS=b ID=c #d}
.
<p><span class="a b" ID="d">x</span></p>
```

```
|>{style="color:red"} a |
.
<table>
  <tbody>
    <tr><td style="color:red; text-align: right;">a</td></tr>
  </tbody>
</table>
```
